ext":"and verification URI are surfaced. §14.3 rule 2 is explicit that an SDK must not print"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them to stdout on the caller’s behalf — a device shows them however it can: a screen, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"QR code, an e-ink panel."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The returned token set is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not adopted"}]},{"type":"text","text":" as this client’s credential. Adoption is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same MAY as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loginClientCredentials"},{"type":"text","text":" (§14.3 rule 4), and this SDK takes one posture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"everywhere: return the tokens, install nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Polling follows §14.2 exactly: the interval starts at the server’s, ","type":"text"},{"code":"slow_down","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" adds 5 s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"permanently, and the loop stops at ","type":"text"},{"code":"expires_in","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" even if the server has not yet said so.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"429 rate_limit_exceeded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (contract 1.64, rule 9) is not terminal and is not a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"slow_down","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the next wait is the longer of the interval and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Retry-After","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", it stands in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for that one interval, the interval itself is unchanged, and when the wait would pass the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deadline the loop raises ","type":"text"},{"code":"expired_token","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" at once and sends nothing after it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}